# /tempora home
tempora.command.home.description=Lists the places a player has spent the most time, busiest first, from their position history. Useful for finding their base, and for telling it apart from an AFK farm or spawn. Each place is the %sx%s chunks around its busiest chunk, and clicking it teleports you to where they last stood there.
tempora.command.home.arg0=Name of the player to look up.
tempora.command.home.arg1=How far back to look, e.g. 1d, 3w, 1mo. A range such as 3w-1w looks between 3 weeks and 1 week ago. Default is everything still stored.
tempora.command.home.arg2=Only look in this dimension, by ID. Default is every dimension.
tempora.command.home.arg3=How many places to list, up to %s, default %s.
tempora.command.home.header=Places %s spent the most time:
tempora.command.home.spot=%s. %s of their time, in %s at %s, last there %s
tempora.command.home.no_more=No other places where they spent much time.
tempora.command.home.no_db=Player position logging is disabled, so there is no position history to search.

